---
import FocusedServicePage from '../components/FocusedServicePage.astro';
const data={
 slug:'b2b-seo-services',name:'B2B SEO Services',metaTitle:'B2B SEO for Consultancies and Service Firms | Bright Forge',description:'B2B SEO for consultancies and service firms: clear capability pages, proof at the decision point and enquiry tracking. See our published Conscient case.',
 heroTitle:'B2B SEO for Businesses That Need <span>to Make the Shortlist</span>',cta:'Discuss Your B2B Website',
 intro:['A business buyer searches several times over weeks, compares a shortlist and consults colleagues before anyone picks up the phone. To stay on that shortlist, your website has to explain the problem you solve, show the organisations you can help and put the evidence behind your offer where a sceptical reader will find it. Traffic to a broad definition page rarely does any of the three.','We help consultancies and B2B service firms organise their search presence around that evaluation. The work connects service capability, relevant sectors and published proof to a clear next step, and it never pretends that every search click is a qualified sales opportunity.'],
 proofTitle:'Consultancy Experience,',proofHighlight:'Not a Generic B2B Claim',
 proofBody:['Our published B2B case is Conscient (conscient.co.uk), a UK B2B marketing consultancy serving telecoms, technology and data-centre buyers, whose services include brand and messaging, content creation and consultancy. The search challenge for a firm like this is to make its consultancy work discoverable without reducing the website to a generic agency brochure.','The published Search Console image compares the last six months with the previous six months: rounded click totals rose from 13.2K to 15.7K and impressions from 398K to 742K, while click-through rate fell from 3.3% to 2.1%. We report the fall as plainly as the rise. Exact calendar dates and country/search filters are not visible. That is search-performance evidence, not proof of a particular sales pipeline or a promised return for another firm.'],
 proofLinks:[{href:'/case-studies/consulting-firm-seo/',label:'Conscient: published consultancy SEO work'},{href:'/case-studies/industrial-parts-washing-search-growth/',label:'Anonymised industrial search-performance example'}],
 sections:[
  {id:'b2b-service-ownership',eyebrow:'Service and Buyer Fit',title:'Explain What You Do',highlight:'Before Expanding the Content',body:['We identify the services you actively sell, the buying problems behind them and the pages that already support those decisions. That usually means talking to the people who sell and deliver the work, because they know the questions buyers actually ask. A long list of industries is no substitute for a credible offer in each one.'],rows:[{title:'Capability Pages',body:'One page per service, written for the person who has the problem. It makes the scope, deliverables and practical fit clear, so a buyer can distinguish advisory work, implementation and ongoing support without opening three interchangeable pages.'},{title:'Problem and Sector Relevance',body:'We use buyer language and examples that your team can stand behind. A new sector page needs its own questions and its own evidence. A copied service description with another industry name on it convinces neither the buyer nor Google.'},{title:'Proof at the Decision Point',body:'We connect the appropriate case studies to service and enquiry pages, and each one explains the situation, the work and its limits. A search metric is never used as a substitute for commercial outcomes that were not measured.'}],links:[{href:'/keyword-research-services/',label:'Buyer and competitor research'},{href:'/seo-audit-services/',label:'Existing-page audit'}]},
  {id:'b2b-shortlist-journey',eyebrow:'From Discovery to Evaluation',title:'Help the Buyer',highlight:'Assess the Next Step',body:['B2B purchases can involve several reviewers. One person may discover the business through a problem query while another checks the capability, the evidence and the contact route. We organise internal links and page content to support that evaluation. Demanding an immediate sales call from every visitor loses the ones who were only sent to check you out.','The plan distinguishes content that explains a problem from pages that sell a service. When an existing page can own the intent, we improve it. Publishing a second page that competes for the same job helps nobody.'],rows:[{title:'Technical Access',body:'Important service and case-study pages must be crawlable, linked and readable in the delivered page. We check the actual site output; a CMS field that looks right is not evidence that the page is.'},{title:'Useful Enquiry Paths',body:'A next step should fit the buying decision: discussing scope, sharing a brief or reviewing the website. We test the route and agree how a relevant enquiry will be identified where the tracking allows it.'}],links:[{href:'/technical-seo-services-philippines/',label:'Technical SEO support'},{href:'/content-seo-services-philippines/',label:'Content planning and delivery'}]},
  {id:'specialist-b2b-boundaries',eyebrow:'Different Businesses, Different Owners',title:'Use Specialist Pages',highlight:'Where the Buying Journey Changes',body:['This offer centres on professional services and consultancy evaluation. Software trials, product catalogues and construction quotes bring different requirements. They should not be hidden inside a generic B2B page or used to imply expertise in every vertical.','We use the relevant specialist scope where it fits, and we confirm the experience and review resources before entering an unfamiliar sector. Published industrial search data provides a supporting example of measurement, not permission to claim undisclosed client work or results.'],links:[{href:'/saas-seo-services/',label:'SaaS, product trials and demos'},{href:'/construction-seo-services/',label:'Construction and industrial buying journeys'},{href:'/ecommerce-seo-services/',label:'Product and catalogue SEO'}]},
  {id:'b2b-engagement',eyebrow:'Scope and Reporting',title:'Agree What Success',highlight:'Can Be Measured Against',body:['We begin with the priority services, target market, existing pages and available evidence. The resulting plan identifies page owners, content requirements, technical dependencies and the first implementation sequence. The written proposal states responsibilities and review points. It does not promise a fixed ranking result.','Reporting separates visibility and clicks from enquiries, demos or opportunities recorded in a reliable system. We do not label traffic as pipeline when that connection is missing. Country and page-level views help distinguish growth in useful discovery from a wider but less relevant query mix, which is the question the Conscient figures raise.','Share the website, the work you want to win and the examples you can publish. We will assess the fit before recommending a broader content programme.']}
 ],
 faqs:[
  {question:'Is B2B SEO the same as SaaS SEO?',answer:'No. SaaS campaigns often involve product features, integrations, comparison pages and trials or demos. This page focuses on how buyers evaluate consultancies and professional-service firms, where the product is the team and its record. We use our separate SaaS scope when the product journey calls for it.'},
  {question:'Do you guarantee qualified leads?',answer:'No. Search visibility is only one part of acquisition. We work on the relevant pages and enquiry paths, but lead quality also depends on the offer, the market, qualification and your sales process. Commercial outcomes are reported only where they can be measured reliably.'},
  {question:'Do we need separate pages for every industry?',answer:'Only where the service, the buyer questions and the credible evidence differ enough to justify them. We review existing ownership first. An unsupported list of sector pages creates duplication without helping a buyer assess fit.'},
  {question:'Can you work with our internal subject experts?',answer:'Yes, and the work is better for it. Your team supplies the technical and commercial knowledge that keeps service claims accurate. We agree review responsibilities and approval points before any reader-facing content or implementation is released.'},
  {question:'Can the campaign cover more than one country?',answer:'It can, where you have a viable offer and the resources to support those markets. We separate country research and measurement, and use international SEO planning when regional architecture or country-page ownership needs work.'}
 ]
};
---
<FocusedServicePage data={data} />
